  "worked_solution": "From the equation of a plane in the parametric form $r=p+tv+sw$, we have that its normal vector is $n=v\\times w.$ In our case, the normal vectors to $\u03a0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =\u27e81,0,4\u27e9\\times \u27e82,6,0\u27e9 \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =-24i+8j+6k \\\\  & =\u27e8-24,8,6\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane $\u03a0$ in dot product form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot \u27e8-24,8,6\u27e9 & =\u27e8-12,10,6\u27e9\\cdot \u27e8-24,8,6\u27e9 \\\\ r\\cdot \u27e8-24,8,6\u27e9 & =404.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=\u27e81,3,2\u27e9+w\u27e8-5,-2,-1\u27e9$ into the equation of the plane in dot product form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot \u27e8-24,8,6\u27e9 & =404 \\\\ \u27e81-5w,3-2w,2-w\u27e9\\cdot \u27e8-24,8,6\u27e9 & =404 \\\\ -24(1-5w)+8(3-2w)+6(2-w) & =404 \\\\ -24+120w+24-16w+12-6w & =404 \\\\ 98w & =392 \\\\ w & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $q$ of the intersection point $Q,$ we substitute $w=4$ into the vector equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q & =\u27e81-5(4),3-2(4),2-(4)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8-19,-5,-2\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $Q(-19,-5,-2).$",
